        <mxCell id="b64" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=8;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:8px;color:#666666&quot;&gt;0.03%&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="90" x="193" y="1196" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b65" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f9f9f9;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1a1a1a;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Relationships&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;#9472;&amp;#9472;&amp;#9472;&lt;/b&gt; solid &amp;mdash; foreign key enforced by Db2 (3 constraints declared in &lt;i&gt;02_tables.sql&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#9673A6&quot;&gt;&amp;#9548;&amp;#9548;&amp;#9548;&lt;/b&gt; dashed &amp;mdash; logical join only. The columns line up and queries join on them, but no constraint enforces it, so orphans are possible and must be checked in silver.&lt;br&gt;Single bar = exactly one &amp;nbsp;&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; circle + bar = zero or one &amp;nbsp;&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; circle + crow&amp;#39;s foot = zero or many.&lt;br&gt;Optionality is drawn as the DDL enforces it: a NOT NULL foreign key makes the child&amp;#39;s parent mandatory, but nothing obliges a customer to hold a card.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Column markers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#7F3300&quot;&gt;PK&lt;/b&gt; primary key &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b style=&quot;color:#10739E&quot;&gt;FK&lt;/b&gt; foreign key &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b style=&quot;color:#666666&quot;&gt;WM&lt;/b&gt; watermark column&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Volume tiers&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;(header colour)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Green &amp;mdash; reference, under 1K rows&lt;br&gt;Blue &amp;mdash; master, 1K to 10K rows&lt;br&gt;Orange &amp;mdash; high volume, over 1M rows&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reading the model.&lt;/b&gt; Three tables hold 99.97% of the rows and none of them is a dimension &amp;mdash; this is a narrow-and-deep transactional estate, which is why the demo is about throughput and exact control totals rather than modelling. Only 35 of 61 columns are shown; the full definitions live in &lt;i&gt;db2/ddl/02_tables.sql&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;db2/ddl/03_tables_optional.sql&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources.&lt;/b&gt; Structure from &lt;i&gt;db2/ddl/01_schema.sql&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;02_tables.sql&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;03_tables_optional.sql&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;overlay.json&lt;/i&gt;; row counts from &lt;i&gt;docs/session-handoff.md&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;docs/runbook-phase1.md&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="495" width="380" x="920" y="730" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="QuxONXoqReRvFrAymYQP-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f9f9f9;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1a1a1a;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Relationships&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;#9472;&amp;#9472;&amp;#9472;&lt;/b&gt; solid &amp;mdash; foreign key enforced by Db2 (3 constraints declared in &lt;i&gt;02_tables.sql&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#9673A6&quot;&gt;&amp;#9548;&amp;#9548;&amp;#9548;&lt;/b&gt; dashed &amp;mdash; logical join only. The columns line up and queries join on them, but no constraint enforces it, so orphans are possible and must be checked in silver.&lt;br&gt;Single bar = exactly one &amp;nbsp;&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; circle + bar = zero or one &amp;nbsp;&amp;middot;&amp;nbsp; circle + crow&amp;#39;s foot = zero or many.&lt;br&gt;Optionality is drawn as the DDL enforces it: a NOT NULL foreign key makes the child&amp;#39;s parent mandatory, but nothing obliges a customer to hold a card.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Column markers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#7F3300&quot;&gt;PK&lt;/b&gt; primary key &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b style=&quot;color:#10739E&quot;&gt;FK&lt;/b&gt; foreign key &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b style=&quot;color:#666666&quot;&gt;WM&lt;/b&gt; watermark column&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Volume tiers&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;(header colour)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Green &amp;mdash; reference, under 1K rows&lt;br&gt;Blue &amp;mdash; master, 1K to 10K rows&lt;br&gt;Orange &amp;mdash; high volume, over 1M rows&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reading the model.&lt;/b&gt; Three tables hold 99.97% of the rows and none of them is a dimension &amp;mdash; this is a narrow-and-deep transactional estate, which is why the demo is about throughput and exact control totals rather than modelling. Only 35 of 61 columns are shown; the full definitions live in &lt;i&gt;db2/ddl/02_tables.sql&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;db2/ddl/03_tables_optional.sql&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources.&lt;/b&gt; Structure from &lt;i&gt;db2/ddl/01_schema.sql&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;02_tables.sql&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;03_tables_optional.sql&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;overlay.json&lt;/i&gt;; row counts from &lt;i&gt;docs/session-handoff.md&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;docs/runbook-phase1.md&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="495" width="380" x="930" y="740" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
